              {
                "id": "F8",
                "statement": "What tells the alerts apart: as indicators they look alike (6 senders and 6 transfers in one hour each). The recorded relationships differ in three ways. (a) Pass-through: A-9278 passed on all of its contributions, each batch within 1,800,000 ms, through a fixed 3-hop route (A-5092, A-2897, A-4989) with small drops in amount at each hop. A-9895 passed on only 3 of its 6 contributions, over 1 hop. (b) Shared device: A-9278's route shares D-568 across three sending accounts; A-9895's route shares no device. (c) Amounts: A-9278 received varied amounts totalling 357000; A-9895 received six identical 2500 transfers totalling 15000. So A-9278's alert sits inside a recorded multi-hop, single-device relay pattern, while A-9895's alert is a small, uniform fan-in with limited recorded onward movement.",
